00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.420
I hope you enjoy living alone with your precious knife!

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:42.810
Ronja and Birk got into a fight over something completely trivial.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.530
However, they were able to make up with each other

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.490
when they rescued an injured wild horse in the forest.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.570
Birk told Ronja what he'd come to realize:

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.300
"You're more important to me than a thousand knives!"

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.510
With the Wild Horses

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.510
With the Wild Horses

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.700
As the days passed, spring turned to summer,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.020
bringing warmth to the forest.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.060
The rain came pouring down upon the treetops.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.820
For days and nights it drizzled on...

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:15.200
Until the trees had drunk themselves fresher and greener than ever before.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:55.030
Ronja couldn't help but ask Birk,

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:01.950
"Do you think any other forest on the earth smells as sweet as ours does?"

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:10.170
"No, I don't think so," Birk replied.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.890
Lia!

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.270
Hey! Lia!

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.040
I didn't get much.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:51.070
Yeah...

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.440
Oh!

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.850
It's Rascal and Reckless!

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.950
Rascal! Reckless! Stop it!

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.470
Go away!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.540
You two are nothing but trouble!

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:44.180
They're just wondering what's going on.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.770
Milking isn't commonplace in the wild.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:06.410
When I said I wanted to ride, I meant it!

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.460
You really <i>are</i> a Rascal.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:03.510
But I'll ride you one day, you'll see!

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.730
And she did indeed.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:23.030
Every evening after the milking was finished,

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:30.410
Ronja and Birk tried to teach Rascal and Reckless better manners.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.890
Okay? Understand? You don't need to be afraid.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.850
Can't you be a little more gentle?

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:16.790
See? Look at this!

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.790
I have some too!

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.250
Look at all of this!

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:11.600
However, none of their lessons had any effect.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:18.560
Now there's not one bit of my body that doesn't hurt.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.270
It's your fault that I ache like this!

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:24.530
You scoundrel!

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.400
Look, Ronja!

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:33.830
He's standing still!

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.370
Good boy, Reckless.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:45.500
You're the best horse in the forest, better than any other horse!

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:54.220
Oh please, deep down you know he's still a scoundrel.

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:40.100
Birk keeps making me do all the milking.

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:59.040
You know, you're not the only one who can ride a horse.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:17.930
Birk!

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.020
You'll wait 'till I'm finished milking!

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:23.270
Then you'll see some riding!

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:45.120
Ronja!

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.130
Follow her!

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:52.840
Help me!

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:55.430
He's going to take me all the way to Hell's Gap!

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:56.930
Help!

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.960
Don't let go of the horse!

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:28.130
Go!

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:37.890
Stop!

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:02.080
You ran very well, Rascal.

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:07.710
But I was <i>this</i> close to smacking you on the nose.

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:10.960
It's a miracle that I'm still alive.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:17.970
It's a bigger miracle that we're both riding.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:24.100
We've tamed them.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:29.600
Did I really tame you?

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:41.160
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:41.160
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.760
Hey Birk,

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:08.640
have you noticed that Lia's been giving less milk?

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:10.390
Yeah...

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:14.310
She'll have a new foal on the way before long.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:18.650
Soon she'll dry up altogether.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:24.160
Then we'll be living off spring water again.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.950
And soon we'll have to manage without bread too.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:37.380
Even without bread or Lia's milk, we won't starve to death.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:42.130
There are plenty of fish and birds in the forest.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:47.060
Plus, we have the plants and herbs you gathered too.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:58.480
No, we won't starve.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:05.620
But I couldn't stand how that first day was, with no milk or bread...

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:09.200
I can't live like that.

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:18.460
However, that day came much sooner than they'd expected.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:25.180
Getting anything?

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:29.140
All I could get was a few drops.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:30.470
I see...

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:37.650
Lia, thanks for all the milk.

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:42.110
You'll have a new foal by next summer.

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:43.700
Do you know that?

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:48.700
And then you will have milk again.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:53.410
But that milk's for your foal.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.580
Not for us.

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.670
You should thank Lia too, Birk.

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:04.720
Of course.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.430
Thank you, Lia.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:18.860
Now, go to the others.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:21.920
We found a roaring waterfall!

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:23.050
Yeah.

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:28.180
If we got sucked into that, it'd be the end of the line.

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:42.110
Found ya, tasty little humans!

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:44.480
I'll drink your blood!

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:46.320
A wild harpy!

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:47.320
Run!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:05.630
Ronja! Let's jump!

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:07.130
Alright!

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:19.560
They'll be fine.

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:22.980
The wild harpies don't attack the forest creatures.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:26.070
They only go after humans, huh?

00:18:54.680 --> 00:19:00.650
Where's that pretty little black-haired human?

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.480
I'll dig her eyes out with my claws!

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:21.160
Where's that pretty little black-haired human?

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:27.250
Where'd that tasty little red-haired human run off to?

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:39.260
Hateful humans, I'll let my vicious sisters know about you!

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:52.650
Ronja!

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:54.570
Ronja!

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:01.080
Ronja!

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.450
Birk!

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.290
We made it!

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:14.470
We weren't clawed to death or carried off back to their cave!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.680
You shouldn't be frightened in Mattis' forest!

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:26.390
But with wild harpies circling overhead, it's difficult not to be.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:43.830
We sure did get those horses to run far.

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:49.670
I don't mind walking through the night though.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:52.460
As long as we don't run into any more wild harpies.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:56.110
Even if there are vicious wild harpies around,

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:59.970
I think it's a wonderful thing that we live in the forest.

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:01.890
Of course it is.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.810
We're free here.

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:07.940
Morning, noon, night... Even the sun, and the moon,

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:11.730
and all the stars in the sky are always beautiful here.

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:12.860
Yeah.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:14.820
The springtime sure was nice.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:17.490
And the summer's been great too.

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:18.990
Autumn will be fine.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:23.240
But in winter...

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:36.300
Ronja!

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:57.940
Shadow Folk...

00:21:58.780 --> 00:22:02.990
They'll go on living quite cheerfully, even in wintertime.

00:22:06.040 --> 00:22:09.580
It's still summer right now, sister.

00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:20.630
I'll keep the memory of this summer in my heart for the rest of my life.

00:22:31.390 --> 00:22:33.020
This summer...

00:22:35.980 --> 00:22:43.030
I'll always remember this summer, till the day I die.

00:22:43.620 --> 00:22:45.030
Without a doubt.

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:54.630
When they got home to the Bear's Cave, someone unexpected sat waiting for them on the platform outside.

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:02.140
Lil-Klippen!

00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:10.520
It was Lil-Klippen of Mattis' Robbers.

